{
  "case_id": "2018-17-1077",
  "document_hash": "9a3474b91db94aabe703d9faa8953368ec324be4b0faa879e076832027797b52",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Robert Heim, on behalf of the Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1077",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3474b91db94aabe703d9faa8953368ec324be4b0faa879e076832027797b52",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3474b91db9-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In Janus Capital, this Court held that only the maker of a misstatement can be held liable for that misstatement under Section 10(b) and Rule 10b-5(b). The court below correctly held that Petitioner, Frank Lorenzo, was not the maker of the statements that are at issue in the two emails in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Robert Heim, on behalf of the Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1077",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3474b91db94aabe703d9faa8953368ec324be4b0faa879e076832027797b52",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3474b91db9-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For three reasons Lorenzo's actions do not support liability. First, permitting liability under Rule 10b-5(a) and (c) and 17(a) would allow plaintiffs to sidestep this Court's holding in Janus and the limitations that were placed on misstatement liability."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1077",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3474b91db94aabe703d9faa8953368ec324be4b0faa879e076832027797b52",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3474b91db9-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Excuse me, Janus was a private cause of action, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1077",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3474b91db94aabe703d9faa8953368ec324be4b0faa879e076832027797b52",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3474b91db9-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I tell you, all the content -- I mean, the email begins with a"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1077",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3474b91db94aabe703d9faa8953368ec324be4b0faa879e076832027797b52",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3474b91db9-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HEIM: Well, Justice Sotomayor, just to be clear, our position, as was the D.C. Circuit, was that Mr. Lorenzo was not the maker of -- of these statements."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1077",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3474b91db94aabe703d9faa8953368ec324be4b0faa879e076832027797b52",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3474b91db9-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Can I ask you just some basic questions? The -- there's no doubt, is there, that at the time this email was sent, Lorenzo knew full well that the company was worthless?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1077",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3474b91db94aabe703d9faa8953368ec324be4b0faa879e076832027797b52",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3474b91db9-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What does \"fraud\" mean, other than trying -- doing something to -- to create in the mind of the hearer or recipient a false belief that is material?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1077",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3474b91db94aabe703d9faa8953368ec324be4b0faa879e076832027797b52",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3474b91db9-0002-0002",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And that would, we submit, tear a big loophole in securities fraud law, and that would be a very damaging result for the Commission that I don't think Congress intended and that I don't think is within the ordinary meaning of the text here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1077",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3474b91db94aabe703d9faa8953368ec324be4b0faa879e076832027797b52",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3474b91db9-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Is there a distinction between conduct and statement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1077",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3474b91db94aabe703d9faa8953368ec324be4b0faa879e076832027797b52",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3474b91db9-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 12:04 p.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
